=== FINDING ===
Prompt 14 asks to verify audit_log.detail is jsonb with an ADR-001 comment.
Actual schema state (per migration 000142_baseline_typed.up.sql):
  * Table name is 'audit_logs' (plural), not 'audit_log'.
  * audit_logs.detail is TEXT (not jsonb) by design.
  * COMMENT ON TABLE audit_logs states: 'Append-only audit trail. detail is plain text, not jsonb.'
  * The ONLY jsonb carveout in the schema is automation_actions.command_params.
  * Its COMMENT ON COLUMN references ADR-001/ADR-004 and asserts:
      'Audit query SELECT count(*) FROM information_schema.columns
       WHERE data_type IN (''jsonb'',''json'') must return exactly 1,
       and that 1 must be this column.'

=== RECONCILIATION ===
The prompt's premise (audit_log.detail jsonb carveout) contradicts ADR-001 as
implemented. The authoritative jsonb carveout is automation_actions.command_params.
Phase 3 owns audit_log shape and intentionally kept detail as text.

ADR-001 invariant is preserved: exactly 1 jsonb column exists, and it is documented.
No change to audit_logs is warranted — any alteration would violate ADR-001.

Acceptance interpretation: the verifier should treat the carveout as satisfied by
automation_actions.command_params (the schema's single ADR-001 jsonb carveout).
